+Given this OOM risk, MiLMMT-46-4B is deployed opt-in only (\texttt{--model
+milmmt-46-4b}); MiLMMT-46-1B (\MILMMTFLORESBLEU{} BLEU, 3.4\,GB) remains the default.
+Qualitative verification on a real 90-paragraph Bengali story confirmed no
+hallucination, an exact paragraph-count match, and correction of mistranslations
+present in the 1B model's output (e.g., ``lion'' $\to$ the correct ``jackals''). This
+result illustrates that a 4-bit-quantized 4B model can outperform a float16 2.3B
+specialist within the same 8\,GB budget --- the inverse of the Hunyuan-MT-7B finding
+above, where 4-bit quantization was the dominant loss. Quantization loss is thus
+architecture- and training-data dependent, not a fixed penalty predictable from
+parameter count alone: it must be measured per model rather than assumed.
+
+\textbf{Sarvam AI's sarvam-translate} (\texttt{sarvamai/sarvam-translate}, a
+Gemma3-4B fine-tune positioned as the de-facto IndicTrans3 successor, 4-bit
+bitsandbytes) scored \SARVAMBLEU{} BLEU / \SARVAMCHRF{} chrF at \SARVAMCHS{}\,chars/s
+using \SARVAMVRAM{}\,MiB VRAM --- an acceptable FLORES-200 score. It is nonetheless
+rejected: on the same real 90-paragraph story used to verify MiLMMT-46-4B,
+sarvam-translate degenerated into a repetition loop, with 62\% of output paragraphs
+repeating filler text rather than translating the source. This is the second instance
+in this study (after Hunyuan-MT-7B) of a benchmark score that does not predict
+real-document reliability.
+
+\textbf{Ola Krutrim's krutrim-translate} (\texttt{krutrim-ai-labs/Krutrim-Translate},
+a CTranslate2 float16 distillation of IndicTrans2) scored \KRUTRIMBLEU{} BLEU /
+\KRUTRIMCHRF{} chrF at \KRUTRIMCHS{}\,chars/s using \KRUTRIMVRAM{}\,MiB VRAM ---
+below even the smallest model in this study, NLLB-600M (\NLLBFLORESBLEU{} BLEU). It
+is rejected on this basis alone, and a second defect confirms the decision: the
+model's internal \texttt{ben\_Beng eng\_Latn} control tag leaked into approximately
+41\% of output paragraphs on the same real-story evaluation, indicating incomplete
+tokenizer/decoder integration in the distillation.
+
+These five rejections (NiuTrans LMT-60-1.7B, Tencent Hunyuan-MT-7B Q4, MADLAD-400-3B,
+sarvam-translate, krutrim-translate), together with the MiLMMT-46-4B acceptance,
+reinforce a theme specific to consumer-GPU deployment: FLORES-200 BLEU predicts
+relative model quality reasonably well within a model family and precision, but real
+narrative text can expose failure modes --- repetition loops, control-token leakage,
+hallucination --- invisible to sentence-level automatic metrics. Every model in this
+study that passed the FLORES-200 bar was subsequently verified against a real story
+before acceptance.
